course: dictionary
lesson: 2573
title: Demand: a firm ask, a need, or what people want
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Demand is a word with more than one meaning, so check which one fits the sentence. In «She demanded an answer», demanded means she asked for one firmly, as if she had the right to it. In «The job demands patience», demands means the job needs patience.
explain: As a noun, a demand is a firm request, like «A final demand is a warning that a bill is very overdue». Demand can also mean how much people want something, as in «Jobs that need rare skills are in demand.»
explain: Use the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense. Asking nicely works better than demanding rudely: «Give me that!» is not polite.
fact: Demand can be a verb (to demand) or a noun (a demand).
fact: «Demand» as a verb means to ask for something firmly, as if you have the right to it.
fact: «Demand» can also mean need: «the job demands patience» means the job needs patience.
fact: «In demand» means many people want something.
fact: In supply and demand, when demand is high and supply is low, prices often go up.
exercise: In «She demanded an answer», what does demanded mean? | Forgot about | Laughed at | *Asked for firmly, as if she had the right to one | Whispered quietly
exercise: What does demands mean in «The job demands patience»? | Pays for | Forgets | *Needs | Refuses
exercise: «Jobs with rare skills are in demand.» What does in demand mean? | *Many people want them | Nobody wants them | They are very old | They are cheap
test: In supply and demand, what does demand describe? | How old a product is | The number of shops in a town | *How much people want to buy something | How fast a price changes
test: Why is asking nicely better than demanding rudely? | *It is more polite, so people are more willing to help | It is faster | It costs less | Rude words are longer
exam: What does demanded mean in «The children demanded to know who had won»? | Forgot the answer | Asked for a gift | *Asked for firmly, as if they had the right to know | Needed sleep
